Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:18:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NavRelay: keep server alive across Pi reconnects, rebind
 listener

- NavServer: a write error (Pi disconnected, e.g. dashboard restarted)
  no longer stops the server; it drops the client and keeps accepting.
  Server restarts itself on errors; exposes state for the UI.
- MapsNotificationListener: track bind state, request rebind after
  updates, never drop a Maps notification silently (fallback action).
- MainActivity: live status (notification access, listener bound,
  Bluetooth server, messages sent, last parsed info).
- main.c: restore "Nav updated" terminal log.

